;;; A count of commitments past what the run holds is an exit 1 with no read-out
;;; — M1f **W92**, register row `W92/count-past-2-64` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`),
;;; filed by S1f.6.25 (T1f.6.25.5, 2026-11-13) from E-22 of P1f.6's
;;; `findings.md`.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; 64 items, one open relation over them, `chosen`, and one rule: if any
;;; item is chosen, every item is. So there are 64 candidates, `(chosen x1)`
;;; to `(chosen x64)`, and two states: ∅, and ⊤ with all 64 chosen, which
;;; every commitment but the empty one reaches.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Nothing is refuted and nothing is owed, so R is every commitment: two
;;; states, ∅ and ⊤, and 2^64 commitments, 1 that reaches ∅ and 2^64 − 1
;;; that reach ⊤, each of the 64 one-candidate sets a minimal one. The run
;;; classifies every commitment after 65 saturations, so the description
;;; is exhausted. A count past 2^63 − 1 is reported as *9 223 372 036 854 775
;;; 807 or more*: that is an answer, and it exits 0.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `5e5685b7`, release: one line on stderr, *a state's commitments pass
;;; 2^128: the state route cannot count them*, nothing on stdout, exit 1,
;;; from a bare `ein solve`, `--count` and `--json-summary`; `--minimal` and
;;; `--maximal` answered. No claim was refuted and the program is not in
;;; error, and what the run had established, both states and both lines, was
;;; lost. The sentence was not true of this
;;; program either: its count is 2^64, which passed the `u64` the total was
;;; summed into, not 2^128. 64 items is the smallest size that met it.

(relation chosen Thing :why "{?1} is chosen")

(rule all ()
  :match  (and (chosen ?x) (item ?y))
  :assert (chosen ?y)
  :why    "{?x} is chosen, so {?y} is")

(item x1) (item x2) (item x3) (item x4) (item x5) (item x6) (item x7) (item x8)
(item x9) (item x10) (item x11) (item x12) (item x13) (item x14) (item x15) (item x16)
(item x17) (item x18) (item x19) (item x20) (item x21) (item x22) (item x23) (item x24)
(item x25) (item x26) (item x27) (item x28) (item x29) (item x30) (item x31) (item x32)
(item x33) (item x34) (item x35) (item x36) (item x37) (item x38) (item x39) (item x40)
(item x41) (item x42) (item x43) (item x44) (item x45) (item x46) (item x47) (item x48)
(item x49) (item x50) (item x51) (item x52) (item x53) (item x54) (item x55) (item x56)
(item x57) (item x58) (item x59) (item x60) (item x61) (item x62) (item x63) (item x64)
